// wdoc section: Wireframe UI Widgets.
page wdoc_wireframe { sites = [:reference]
  h1 "Wireframe UI Widgets"

  p "Wireframe widgets render UI mockups — windows, buttons, inputs, controls — as styled HTML. Unlike diagram shapes (which lower to flat SVG leaves), widgets render through the HTML path and **container widgets nest other widgets**, so you can compose a window of panels of rows of controls."

  h2 "Window"

  p "`wf_window` is the top-level widget: a titlebar with optional traffic-light controls plus a body that hosts other widgets."

  code wcl {
    source = <<'WCL'
wf_window "Account settings" {
  wf_panel {
    title = "Profile"
    wf_input "Display name" { value = "Wil Taylor" }
    wf_input "Email"        { value = "ai@wiltaylor.dev" }
  }
  wf_row {
    wf_button "Cancel"
    wf_button "Save" { class = ["primary"] }
  }
}
WCL
  }

  h2 "Containers"

  table {
    rows:
      | "Widget"      | "Purpose" |
      | "`wf_window`" | "Outer chrome — titlebar + body. `controls = false` hides the traffic lights." |
      | "`wf_panel`"  | "Bordered group with an optional `title` caption." |
      | "`wf_column`" | "Stack children vertically (default flow inside a panel)." |
      | "`wf_row`"    | "Stack children horizontally." |
      | "`wf_grid`"   | "Two-dimensional grid; takes `columns` (and optionally `rows`)." |
  }

  p "Every container accepts `@children(Widget)` — drop any other widget inside, nested arbitrarily."

  h2 "Leaf controls"

  table {
    rows:
      | "Widget"        | "Inline label" | "Other fields" |
      | "`wf_label`"    | "the text"     | "—" |
      | "`wf_button`"   | "the caption"  | "`icon` (e.g. `\"lucide.check\"`)" |
      | "`wf_input`"    | "the placeholder" | "`value` (fills with solid text)" |
      | "`wf_dropdown`" | "the placeholder" | "`value`" |
      | "`wf_checkbox`" | "the label"    | "`checked` (bool)" |
      | "`wf_radio`"    | "the label"    | "`selected` (bool)" |
      | "`wf_toggle`"   | "the label"    | "`on` (bool)" |
  }

  h2 "Common fields"

  p "Every widget extends a shared `Widget` interface and accepts:"

  table {
    rows:
      | "Field"      | "Meaning" |
      | "`id`"       | "Optional HTML id." |
      | "`class`"    | "Extra CSS classes — see Styling below." |
      | "`width`"    | "Explicit CSS width (e.g. `\"12rem\"` / `\"100%\"`)." |
      | "`disabled`" | "When `true`, adds a `wf-disabled` class so styles can dim the control." |
  }

  h2 "Styling"

  p "Every widget threads its `class` field onto the rendered element and paints from a bare class — `.wf-button`, `.wf-window`, `.wf-input`, etc. The bundled `wdoc-wireframe` stylesheet seeds a clean grey-box palette via `--wf-*` custom properties (dark default + light override + theme-toggle override). Two override paths:"

  code wcl {
    source = <<'WCL'
// Recolour every wireframe button:
class "wf-button" {
  background = "var(--wdoc-accent)"
  color      = "#fff"
}

// Or a one-off variant on a single instance:
class primary {
  background = "var(--wdoc-accent)"
  bold       = true
}

wf_button "Save" { class = ["primary"] }
WCL
  }

  callout "Mockups, not interactivity" {
    class = ["info"]
    body  = "Wireframe widgets are visual mockups — they render as styled <div>s and don't respond to clicks. For runnable terminal-style UI, see TUI Widgets."
  }

  p "Back to the [reference introduction](index)."
}
